h: computed rotated pin positions for J1 (180 deg), R1 and C1, traced every wire and label; confirmed J1.1=/IN->R1.1, R1.2=/OUT=C1.1=J1.2, C1.2=GND=J1.3, matching work/netlist/design.xml and work/netlist/connectivity.json.\",\"ERC record (work/erc/erc.json, console.log, execution.json): zero violations on 1 sheet; PWR_FLAG present on GND so power-input pin checks are legitimately satisfied; ignored-check list reviewed and none is relevant to this 3-component passive design.\",\"PCB pad-to-net assignment in inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb cross-checked against the netlist for all 7 pads (C1.1/C1.2, R1.1/R1.2, J1.1/J1.2/J1.3); consistent with DRC schematic-parity result of 0 issues (work/drc/drc.json).\",\"Board copper connectivity traced by coordinates: /IN track (100,100)-(104.0875,100) joins J1.1 to R1.1; /OUT tracks join R1.2, C1.1 and J1.2; GND track (110.95,100)-(113,100) joins C1.2 to the GND via at (113,100); via and J1.3 thermal spokes verified present inside the saved B.Cu filled_polygon; consistent with 0 unconnected items in DRC and geometry probe.\",\"Geometry requirement (min 0.2 mm track width) independently confirmed from the native board file: all five (segment ...) items carry (width 0.25); via width 0.6 mm; zone min_thickness 0.25 mm; matches work/geometry/geometry.json narrowest 0.25 mm.\",\"Transient verification audited: deck (work/rc-step/deck.cir) matches netlist element values and nodes (C1 OUT-0 100n, R1 IN-OUT 10k, GND mapped to node 0, connector J1 correctly carries no element); stimulus PWL(0 0 1n 1) is an adequate ideal 1 V step; .tran 5us/5ms resolution sufficient; measured vout_1ms=0.6321201 V equals analytic 1-exp(-1)=0.632121 V within interpolation error and lies inside the declared 0.62-0.65 V band; vout_5ms=0.9932621 V matches 1-exp(-5); log (work/rc-step/ngspice.log) and recorded measurements agree; ngspice invoked with -n -b (not -b -r), so .meas execution is trustworthy.\",\"Hash consistency: board_sha256 in DRC and geometry details matches inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb sha256; console sha256 values match the included console.log artifacts.\",\"Board outline and clearances sanity-checked: 20x12 mm Edge.Cuts rectangle encloses all footprints, tracks, via and the zone outline (0.5 mm inset from edge).\"],\"limitations\":[\"Text-only review without tools: work/rc-step/result.raw (binary) was not inspected; measurement values were taken from work/rc-step/ngspice.log and the check record, which are mutually consistent.\",\"Zone connectivity to J1 pad 3 and the GND via was verified from the saved filled_polygon vertices plus DRC/probe unconnected-item counts; no independent refill or polygon re-computation was possible (refill forbidden by the read-only candidate, per declared limitations).\",\"Stock library symbol/footprint source files were not included in the packet; footprint pad geometry was taken from the embedded copies in rc_filter.kicad_pcb.\",\"Per the declared scope, tolerance, temperature, external loading, ADC sampling, EMI and physical hardware behavior were not evaluated; only the stated ideal unloaded step condition was reviewed.\",\"ERC/DRC correctness is taken from the kicad-cli 10.0.7 JSON reports; I verified their inputs and plausibility but cannot re-run the checkers.\"],\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"geo-probe-assert-noise\",\"title\":\"Geometry probe emitted pcbnew PROPERTY_ENUM assertion failures on stderr\",\"location\":\"work/geometry/console.log\",\"condition\":\"The geometry probe console shows three repeated assertions: 'assert \\\"m_choices.GetCount() > 0\\\" failed in PROPERTY_ENUM(): No enum choices defined' while loading the board, although the probe exited 0 and produced complete output.\",\"mechanism\":\"Assertion noise from the pcbnew Python bindings indicates the tool ran in a partially degraded or debug-assert configuration; in principle such internal errors could accompany incomplete property extraction, which would silently weaken a width/geometry scan.\",